# doc-sections — advice the vendored doc-check.sh prints on a hit
# (shipping-work-python-fastapi Step 1.5). One doc section per line; blank
# lines and `#`-comments ignored. This file REPLACES the script's built-in
# defaults rather than extending them (gregoryfoster/skills#261, #173).
#
# .skills/doc-sensitive-paths says what the gate watches; this says which docs
# to spot-check when one of those paths changes. Keep the two in step: a doc
# that starts mirroring a path's inventory belongs here AND its path belongs in
# the list. Upstream runs no dead-entry check on advice, since it is prose, so
# tests/test_doc_sensitive_paths.py asserts each line opens with `<doc>:` naming
# a tracked file.

AGENTS.md: architecture diagram, frozen/derived table, conventions, infra + env tables, common tasks, skills
README.md: Features, Project Structure tree, API Endpoints tables, Testing file table, CLI commands in Setup and ops sections
docs/SCHEMA.md: table/column reference (models.py, alembic/versions/)
docs/MIGRATIONS.md: Alembic revision history (alembic/versions/)
docs/MEMORY_PRESSURE.md: memory configs + SocratiCode pins (infra/, .claude/settings.json)
docs/DEPLOYMENT.md: systemd services and ops reference (infra/)
docs/MONITORING.md: co-status check-ins, the scrape drop-in + monitor fields (infra/wslcb-task@scrape.service.d/, checkin.py)
docs/RELAY.md: relay import + Mac install (relay.py, scripts/relay/, infra/wslcb-task@import-relayed.service.d/)
docs/SKILLS.md: skill descriptions and trigger phrases (skills/)
docs/STYLE.md: brand colors and CSS conventions (static/, templates/)
